FreeToken is an edge-native Mixture-of-Experts serving engine. FreeSwarm is built on
it and does not replace it. For engine documentation, releases, supported models and
updates, go to the upstream project above.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
FreeToken -- native Windows port
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

FreeSwarm derives its copy of the engine from the native-Windows port of FreeToken,
not from upstream directly. The port builds and serves natively on Windows with MSVC
and CUDA, where upstream is Linux-only. See docs/WINDOWS_PORT.md.

  Windows port:      https://github.com/UnsignedChad/freetoken-windows
  Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Modifications
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Per section 4(b) of the Apache License, notice is given that the engine source
redistributed here has been modified relative to the FlashML-org/FreeToken upstream.
The modifications are:

  * the native-Windows port described in docs/WINDOWS_PORT.md (MSVC/CUDA build, Windows
    JIT kernel path, triton-windows in place of Linux triton, tornado for pyzmq
    asyncio under uvicorn's Proactor loop, sglang-kernel dropped), by the port's
    authors; and
  * any subsequent changes made by SignalPop LLC in this repository.

The FreeSwarm platform itself -- ui/ (control plane, message board, swarm runner,
console, sandbox) -- is original work by SignalPop LLC and is not part of FreeToken.

